    ],
    "bottomLine": "For a woodworker who wants a robust steel-frame 14-inch saw with a long warranty, the JWBS-14SFX matches the class leaders on capacity."
  },
  {
    "id": "grizzly-g0555lx",
    "name": "Grizzly G0555LX 14-Inch Deluxe Bandsaw",
    "badge": "Best Value 14-Inch",
    "category": "14 in Cast Iron, 1 HP, 6 in Resaw (12 in with Riser)",
    "amazonUrl": "#",
    "description": "The G0555LX is a classic cast-iron 14-inch band saw at a lower price than the steel-frame saws, and it suits someone who mostly cuts curves and smaller stock. Grizzly lists a 1 HP motor that runs on 110V or 220V, a 13-1/2 inch throat, and a maximum cutting height of 6 inches, which you can raise to 12 inches with Grizzly's optional T25555 riser block kit. Blade speeds are listed as 1,800 and 3,100 feet per minute, the blade is 93-1/2 inches long, and the 14 by 14 inch table sits 43 inches from the floor. Grizzly's own sources disagree on left table tilt, with the product page saying 15 degrees and the spec sheet and support FAQ saying 10 degrees for the LX, so do not count on more than 10. The included blade is a 3/8-inch, 6 TPI hook blade, not a resaw blade.",
